      "explicit_state_columns": [],
      "ledger_semantics": "The source burns credit down by UPDATEing CREDIT_NOTES in place, so it keeps no record of which invoice consumed which note. CREDIT_NOTES belongs to the bronze units and this unit never writes it, so the burn-down is recorded here instead, one row per (invoice, note the sequence visited), carrying the balance the note had when this invoice's sequence reached it, the running counter the source's v_credit held at that point, the amount applied and the balance left. remaining_before is the balance bronze carries minus what this unit's *other* invoices already applied to the note, so a tenant invoiced for two periods burns the same note only once - the source's sequence reads the live table and sees its own earlier applications."
    }
