  "anomalies": [
    "ANOM-GLOBAL-DEPENDENCY",
    "ANOM-HARDCODED-TAX",
    "ANOM-HALF-CENT-TAX",
    "ANOM-CREDIT-OVERAPPLY",
    "ANOM-DYNAMIC-SQL"
  ],
  "reissue_semantics": "reissue_update_columns is the column set a second sp_issue_invoice for the same period actually assigns. Its INSERT hits DUP_VAL_ON_INDEX and the fallback UPDATE sets status_cd only; the UPDATE after the line loop then sets subtotal, tax and total. issued_at is assigned by the INSERT alone, so a re-issued invoice keeps the timestamp of its first issue even though the money moves - the same shape as sp_finalize_rating's re-finalize. Invoice lines are deleted and rebuilt, so every line column is re-assigned.",
  "frozen_status": "silver_invoicing column and type contract; the load and the recon both read this file so the pinned types cannot drift between them (T6, D-23)."
